<article class="env-corollary" id="02BG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02BG">Corollary <span data-tag="02BG">2.3.4.6</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a bicategory, let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ be its coarse homotopy category, and let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ be the functor of Proposition <a data-tag="02AT" href="/tag/02AT">2.2.8.3</a>. Then the induced map of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}(F): \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} ) \]
</div>
<p> exhibits $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ as the homotopy category of the simplicial set $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="004J" href="/tag/004J">1.3.6.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a category, which we regard as a bicategory having only identity morphisms. We wish to show that every morphism of simplicial sets $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ factors uniquely through the morphism $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{D}}(F)$. By virtue of Theorem <a data-tag="00AU" href="/tag/00AU">2.3.4.1</a>, this is equivalent to the assertion that every strictly unital lax functor $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ factors uniquely through $F$, which follows from Proposition <a data-tag="02AT" href="/tag/02AT">2.2.8.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
